    {
      "id": "timonel",
      "fondo": "mar",
      "camara": {
        "de": 0,
        "a": 80,
        "zoom": [
          1,
          1.06
        ]
      },
      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Solo un hombre entendió. Era el timonel, el marinero que maneja el rumbo del barco.",
          "en": "Only one man understood. It was the helmsman, the sailor who steers the ship."
        },
        {
          "es": "Un poeta romano llamado Ovidio cuenta que se llamaba Acetes.",
          "en": "A Roman poet named Ovid says his name was Acoetes."
        },
        {
          "es": "«¡Necios!», gritó. «Este no es un príncipe. ¡Es un dios!»",
          "en": "\"Fools!\" he shouted. \"This is no prince. This is a god!\""
        },
        {
          "es": "«¡Suéltenlo ahora, o nos mandará vientos y tormentas terribles!»",
          "en": "\"Let him go now, or he will send terrible winds and storms against us!\""
        },
        {
          "es": "Pero el capitán se rió. «Ocúpate de la vela, timonel. Este muchacho es nuestro»",
          "en": "But the captain laughed. \"Mind the sail, helmsman. This boy is ours.\""
        }
      ],
